{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Individual Simulation Trace — Module-by-Module Metrics\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo runs **1 agent for 30 days** using the real `StressModel`. After each daily step, it extracts per-phase metrics via `_last_phase_outputs` and organizes them into the 5 modules: stress perception, resilience activation, resource allocation, stress buffering, and daily cycle integration.\n",
        "\n",
        "The theory predicts: challenge/hindrance balance drives stress classification, coping success depends on the C/H ratio modulated by neighbors, resources regenerate with diminishing returns, stress is buffered by available resources, and daily reset pulls affect toward baseline.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "b935818b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from numpy.random import Generator, PCG64\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.model import StressModel\n",
        "from src.python.demos.module_metrics import (\n",
        "    extract_perception_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_activation_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_allocation_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_buffering_metrics,\n",
        "    extract_daily_cycle_metrics,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "_FACTORS = [\"social_support\", \"family_support\", \"formal_intervention\", \"psychological_capital\"]"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Run Loop\n",
        "\n",
        "Single agent, 30 days. For each day, collect all phase outputs via `_last_phase_outputs` and extract metrics for each module."
      ],
      "id": "816f32e6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: run\n",
        "model = StressModel(N=1, max_days=30, seed=42)\n",
        "agent = list(model.agents)[0]\n",
        "\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for day in range(model.max_days):\n",
        "    # Capture pre-state for daily cycle baseline\n",
        "    pre_state = agent._build_agent_state()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Execute one day\n",
        "    model.step()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Read instrumented phase outputs\n",
        "    last = agent._last_phase_outputs\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Module 1: Perception (per stress event) ──\n",
        "    for event in agent.last_daily_stress_events:\n",
        "        # Re-extract perception from the last perception output\n",
        "        perception_out = last.get(\"stress_perception\")\n",
        "        if perception_out is not None:\n",
        "            p_metrics = extract_perception_metrics(perception_out, pre_state)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            p_metrics = None\n",
        "\n",
        "        # ── Module 2: Activation (if stressed) ──\n",
        "        activation_out = last.get(\"resilience_activation\")\n",
        "        a_metrics = extract_activation_metrics(activation_out, pre_state)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Module 3: Allocation ──\n",
        "    alloc_out = last.get(\"resource_allocation\")\n",
        "    alloc_metrics = extract_allocation_metrics(alloc_out, pre_state)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Module 4: Buffering ──\n",
        "    buff_out = last.get(\"stress_buffering\")\n",
        "    buff_metrics = extract_buffering_metrics(buff_out, pre_state)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # ── Module 5: Daily cycle ──\n",
        "    post_state = agent._build_agent_state()\n",
        "    reset_out = last.get(\"daily_reset\")\n",
        "    affect_out = last.get(\"affect_dynamics\")\n",
        "    pss10_out = last.get(\"pss10_consolidation\")\n",
        "    daily_metrics = extract_daily_cycle_metrics(pre_state, post_state, reset_out, affect_out, pss10_out)\n",
        "\n",
        "    n_events = len(getattr(agent, \"last_daily_stress_events\", []))\n",
        "\n",
        "    records.append({\n",
        "        \"day\": day,\n",
        "        \"affect\": agent.affect,\n",
        "        \"resilience\": agent.resilience,\n",
        "        \"resources\": agent.resources,\n",
        "        \"current_stress\": agent.current_stress,\n",
        "        \"pss10\": agent.pss10,\n",
        "        \"n_events\": n_events,\n",
        "        \"n_interactions\": getattr(agent, \"last_daily_interactions\", 0),\n",
        "        \"n_support\": getattr(agent, \"last_daily_support_exchanges\", 0),\n",
        "        # Allocation metrics\n",
        "        \"regeneration_amount\": alloc_metrics[\"regeneration_amount\"] if alloc_metrics else 0,\n",
        "        \"total_allocated\": alloc_metrics[\"total_allocated\"] if alloc_metrics else 0,\n",
        "        # Buffering metrics\n",
        "        \"buffering_strength\": buff_metrics[\"buffering_strength\"] if buff_metrics else 0,\n",
        "        \"stress_depletion\": buff_metrics[\"stress_depletion\"] if buff_metrics else 0,\n",
        "        # Daily cycle metrics\n",
        "        \"affect_reset_magnitude\": daily_metrics[\"affect_reset_magnitude\"] if daily_metrics else 0,\n",
        "        \"stress_decay_amount\": daily_metrics[\"stress_decay_amount\"] if daily_metrics else 0,\n",
        "        # Activation (last event if any)\n",
        "        \"coped_successfully\": a_metrics[\"coped_successfully\"] if a_metrics else None,\n",
        "        # Perception (last event if any)\n",
        "        \"last_challenge\": p_metrics[\"challenge\"] if p_metrics else 0,\n",
        "        \"last_hindrance\": p_metrics[\"hindrance\"] if p_metrics else 0,\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "df_trace = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "print(f\"Recorded {len(df_trace)} days of agent trace\")"
      ],
      "id": "run",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 1 — Stress Perception: Per-Event Breakdown\n",
        "\n",
        "Shows challenge and hindrance for the last event each day."
      ],
      "id": "bb6978a1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-perception\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].scatter(df_trace[\"last_challenge\"], df_trace[\"last_hindrance\"],\n",
        "                c=df_trace[\"day\"], cmap=\"viridis\", alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Challenge (last event)\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Hindrance (last event)\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Challenge vs Hindrance by Day\")\n",
        "axes[0].plot([0, 1], [0, 1], \"k--\", alpha=0.3)\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].hist(df_trace[\"last_challenge\"], alpha=0.6, label=\"challenge\", bins=15)\n",
        "axes[1].hist(df_trace[\"last_hindrance\"], alpha=0.6, label=\"hindrance\", bins=15)\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Appraisal\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Frequency\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Challenge/Hindrance Distribution\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-perception",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 2 — Resilience Activation: Coping Outcome"
      ],
      "id": "63b5e2ce"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-activation\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "coped = df_trace[df_trace[\"coped_successfully\"] == True]\n",
        "not_coped = df_trace[df_trace[\"coped_successfully\"] == False]\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].bar([\"Coped\", \"Not Coped\"],\n",
        "            [len(coped), len(not_coped)],\n",
        "            color=[\"#2ecc71\", \"#e74c3c\"])\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Coping Outcome Count\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if len(coped) > 0 and len(not_coped) > 0:\n",
        "    axes[1].scatter(coped.index, coped[\"resources\"], color=\"#2ecc71\", alpha=0.6, label=\"coped\")\n",
        "    axes[1].scatter(not_coped.index, not_coped[\"resources\"], color=\"#e74c3c\", alpha=0.6, label=\"not coped\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Resources\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Resources by Coping Outcome\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-activation",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 3 — Resource Allocation: PF and Resource Trajectory"
      ],
      "id": "a0b712bd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-allocation\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"resources\"], \"b-\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Resources\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Resources Over Time\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].scatter(df_trace[\"resources\"], df_trace[\"regeneration_amount\"],\n",
        "                c=df_trace[\"day\"], cmap=\"viridis\", alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Resources\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Regeneration Amount\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Regeneration vs Resource Level\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-allocation",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 4 — Stress Buffering: Buffering vs Stress Depletion"
      ],
      "id": "ea7dd78b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-buffering\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].scatter(df_trace[\"buffering_strength\"], df_trace[\"stress_depletion\"],\n",
        "                c=df_trace[\"day\"], cmap=\"RdYlBu_r\", alpha=0.7)\n",
        "axes[0].axhline(0, color=\"grey\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Buffering Strength\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Stress Depletion (resources Δ)\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Buffering vs Depletion\")\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"current_stress\"], \"r-\", linewidth=2, label=\"stress\")\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"buffering_strength\"], \"g-\", linewidth=2, label=\"buffering\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Value\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Stress & Buffering Over Time\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-buffering",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Module 5 — Daily Cycle Integration: Reset & Decay"
      ],
      "id": "6580cf4a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-daily-cycle\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].bar(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"affect_reset_magnitude\"], color=\"steelblue\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Reset Magnitude\")\n",
        "axes[0].set_title(\"Affect Reset Toward Baseline\")\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"affect\"], \"b-\", linewidth=2, label=\"affect\")\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"current_stress\"], \"r-\", linewidth=2, label=\"stress\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Value\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_title(\"Affect & Stress Over Time\")\n",
        "axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-daily-cycle",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Combined State Trajectory\n",
        "\n",
        "Multi-panel view showing all key state variables over the 30-day trace."
      ],
      "id": "079dd126"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-combined\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(12, 8), sharex=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[0].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"affect\"], \"b-\", linewidth=2)\n",
        "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Affect [-1, 1]\"); axes[0].axhline(0, color=\"grey\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.3)\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"resilience\"], \"g-\", linewidth=2, label=\"resilience\")\n",
        "axes[1].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"resources\"], \"orange\", linewidth=2, label=\"resources\")\n",
        "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"[0, 1]\"); axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "axes[2].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"current_stress\"], \"r-\", linewidth=2, label=\"stress\")\n",
        "axes[2].plot(df_trace[\"day\"], df_trace[\"pss10\"] / 40, \"purple\", linewidth=2, label=\"PSS-10/40\")\n",
        "axes[2].set_xlabel(\"Day\"); axes[2].set_ylabel(\"[0, 1]\"); axes[2].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "for ax in axes:\n",
        "    # Mark days with events\n",
        "    event_days = df_trace[df_trace[\"n_events\"] > 0][\"day\"]\n",
        "    for d in event_days:\n",
        "        ax.axvline(d, color=\"red\", alpha=0.08)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.suptitle(\"Single Agent 30-Day State Trajectory\", fontsize=13)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-combined",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What We See\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Perception** drives challenge/hindrance balance: days with hindrance-dominant events precede stress accumulation.\n",
        "- **Activation** determines coping outcome: successful coping preserves resources; failed coping depletes them.\n",
        "- **Allocation** tracks resource regeneration: low-resource days show higher regeneration (diminishing returns).\n",
        "- **Buffering** reduces stress impact proportionally to available resources.\n",
        "- **Daily cycle** resets affect toward baseline and decays stress, preventing indefinite accumulation.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters\n",
        "\n",
        "This trace shows how all 5 modules compose in a single agent over time. The module-by-module breakdown isolates each mechanism's contribution, making it easy to spot anomalies (e.g., reset magnitude too small → stress accumulates across days)."
      ],
      "id": "09e1262a"
    }
  ],
